{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Even"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.one_crossing_not_psd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.one_crossing_not_psd","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L149-L155","doc":"A single `σ₀` is **not** admissible — the convention-D LP's optimum is\nexcluded by the vertex condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.two_crossings_psd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.two_crossings_psd","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L144-L147","doc":"`σ₀²` — the shipped two-crossing gluon term — is admissible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.vertex_psd_iff_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.vertex_psd_iff_even","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L134-L142","doc":"The vertex `σ₀^k` is PSD (both blocks non-negative) iff `k` is even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.altEigenPow_neg_of_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.altEigenPow_neg_of_odd","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L125-L132","doc":"An odd crossing count is excluded. Stated separately because it is the\noperative direction: it is what rules out the single `σ₀` that the\nconvention-D integer-LP re-run returns as its optimum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.altEigenPow_nonneg_iff_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.altEigenPow_nonneg_iff_even","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L109-L123","doc":"**The gluon-vertex parity rule.** For `0 < q`, the alternating projection of\n`σ₀^k` is non-negative exactly when `k` is even — so the `H₂` vertex is PSD\nexactly at an even number of gluon crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.symEigenPow_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.symEigenPow_pos","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L104-L107","doc":"The symmetric block is never the binding constraint: it is positive at\nevery crossing count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.altEigenPow_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.altEigenPow_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L91-L97","doc":"The alternating projection splits into a sign and a magnitude. This is the\nwhole content of the parity rule: the magnitude `(q⁻¹)^k` is positive for\n`0 < q`, so the sign of the projection is the sign of `(-1)^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.altEigenPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.altEigenPow","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L86-L89","doc":"The alternating `(1,1)` block sends `σ₀ ↦ -q⁻¹`, so it sends\n`σ₀^k ↦ (-q⁻¹)^k`. Both projections are ring homomorphisms `H₂(q) → R`, which\nis why a power of the generator maps to the power of its eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.symEigenPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.symEigenPow","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GluonVertexPsdParity.lean#L83-L84","doc":"The symmetric `(2)` block sends `σ₀ ↦ q`, so it sends `σ₀^k ↦ q^k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}